{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1781046629323,"sessionID":"ses_1515955d6ffegNRB71nAdam01t","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"tooluse_W6j2czcSo36qOo9dfp6Tix","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\GHC\\repos\\OMEGA_QUANT\\.ly_state\\session\\p10_l2_gate_tuning_role21_fix_prompt_20260610.md"},"output":"<path>C:\\Users\\GHC\\repos\\OMEGA_QUANT\\.ly_state\\session\\p10_l2_gate_tuning_role21_fix_prompt_20260610.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # [L2-Impl:Role9-BackendEngineer] P10 Gate Tuning Role21 Fix\n2: \n3: You are L2 implementation only. Do not audit/approve.\n4: \n5: ## Scope\n6: Allowed files only:\n7: - `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py`\n8: - `scripts/run_phase35_backtest.py`\n9: - `tests/phase35/test_p10_multi_horizon_blend.py`\n10: - `.ly_state/session/l2_p10_gate_tuning_role21_fix_report_20260610.md`\n11: \n12: ## Read first\n13: - `.ly_state/session/audit_reports/role21_p10_gate_tuning_audit_20260609.md`\n14: \n15: ## Required fixes\n16: \n17: ### F1: Structured fallback-candidate labeling\n18: Problem: relaxed fallback candidates are returned as plain `gated_alphas`, then persisted/metrics can imply they passed Research Gate.\n19: \n20: Implement structured metadata carried from `_compute_horizon_signal()` through P10 horizon details and persisted JSON/fold details.\n21: \n22: Minimum fields per horizon:\n23: - `selection_source`: `research_gate` or `fallback_candidate`\n24: - `used_fallback_candidates`: bool\n25: - `gate_passed_count`: int\n26: - `gate_total`: int\n27: - `gate_required_passes`: int\n28: - `gate_mode`: strict/relaxed\n29: - actual gate-passing alpha list if practical: `gate_passed_alphas`\n30: - selected alpha list can remain `gated_alphas`, but must have source label so fallback-only candidates are not misrepresented.\n31: \n32: Also adjust log wording if easy: avoid saying fallback-only candidates are truly gated; e.g. `Selected alphas` or include source in log.\n33: \n34: Ensure this metadata survives into:\n35: - P10 `horizon_details` / diagnostics\n36: - `FoldMetrics` where relevant\n37: - backtest JSON `fold_details` or equivalent persisted output\n38: \n39: ### F2: Tests\n40: Add tests for:\n41: 1. Relaxed fallback candidates produce `selection_source='fallback_candidate'` and `used_fallback_candidates=True`.\n42: 2. Strict/actual gate pass produces `selection_source='research_gate'` and `used_fallback_candidates=False`.\n43: 3. Persisted/serializable fold diagnostics include the new fields.\n44: 4. CLI flag parse/pass/persist behavior for:\n45:    - `p10_gate_mode`\n46:    - `p10_gate_min_pass`\n47:    - `p10_gate_allow_fallback_candidates`\n48: \n49: If `run_phase35_backtest.py` lacks parser helper, add a small testable helper only if surgical; otherwise test generated JSON config via quick-mode subprocess if existing test style permits.\n50: \n51: ## Verification\n52: Run:\n53: ```powershell\n54: python -m pytest tests/phase35/test_p10_multi_horizon_blend.py -q\n55: python -m pytest tests/phase35/ -q\n56: python scripts/run_phase35_backtest.py --quick-mode --multi-horizon-blend --blend-horizons 1,3,5 --p10-gate-mode relaxed --p10-gate-allow-fallback-candidates\n57: ```\n58: \n59: ## Report\n60: Write `.ly_state/session/l2_p10_gate_tuning_role21_fix_report_20260610.md` mapping F1/F2 to fixes and command results.\n61: \n62: Do not commit/push.\n\n(End of file - total 62 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# [L2-Impl:Role9-BackendEngineer] P10 Gate Tuning Role21 Fix\n\nYou are L2 implementation only. Do not audit/approve.\n\n## Scope\nAllowed files only:\n- `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py`\n- `scripts/run_phase35_backtest.py`\n- `tests/phase35/test_p10_multi_horizon_blend.py`\n- `.ly_state/session/l2_p10_gate_tuning_role21_fix_report_20260610.md`\n\n## Read first\n- `.ly_state/session/audit_reports/role21_p10_gate_tuning_audit_20260609.md`\n\n## Required fixes\n\n### F1: Structured fallback-candidate labeling\nProblem: relaxed fallback candidates are returned as plain `gated_alphas`, then persisted/metrics can imply they passed Research Gate.\n\nImplement structured metadata carried from `_compute_horizon_signal()` through P10 horizon details and persisted JSON/fold details.","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"C:\\Users\\GHC\\repos\\OMEGA_QUANT\\.ly_state\\session\\p10_l2_gate_tuning_role21_fix_prompt_20260610.md","text":"# [L2-Impl:Role9-BackendEngineer] P10 Gate Tuning Role21 Fix\n\nYou are L2 implementation only. Do not audit/approve.\n\n## Scope\nAllowed files only:\n- `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py`\n- `scripts/run_phase35_backtest.py`\n- `tests/phase35/test_p10_multi_horizon_blend.py`\n- `.ly_state/session/l2_p10_gate_tuning_role21_fix_report_20260610.md`\n\n## Read first\n- `.ly_state/session/audit_reports/role21_p10_gate_tuning_audit_20260609.md`\n\n## Required fixes\n\n### F1: Structured fallback-candidate labeling\nProblem: relaxed fallback candidates are returned as plain `gated_alphas`, then persisted/metrics can imply they passed Research Gate.\n\nImplement structured metadata carried from `_compute_horizon_signal()` through P10 horizon details and persisted JSON/fold details.\n\nMinimum fields per horizon:\n- `selection_source`: `research_gate` or `fallback_candidate`\n- `used_fallback_candidates`: bool\n- `gate_passed_count`: int\n- `gate_total`: int\n- `gate_required_passes`: int\n- `gate_mode`: strict/relaxed\n- actual gate-passing alpha list if practical: `gate_passed_alphas`\n- selected alpha list can remain `gated_alphas`, but must have source label so fallback-only candidates are not misrepresented.\n\nAlso adjust log wording if easy: avoid saying fallback-only candidates are truly gated; e.g. `Selected alphas` or include source in log.\n\nEnsure this metadata survives into:\n- P10 `horizon_details` / diagnostics\n- `FoldMetrics` where relevant\n- backtest JSON `fold_details` or equivalent persisted output\n\n### F2: Tests\nAdd tests for:\n1. Relaxed fallback candidates produce `selection_source='fallback_candidate'` and `used_fallback_candidates=True`.\n2. Strict/actual gate pass produces `selection_source='research_gate'` and `used_fallback_candidates=False`.\n3. Persisted/serializable fold diagnostics include the new fields.\n4. CLI flag parse/pass/persist behavior for:\n   - `p10_gate_mode`\n   - `p10_gate_min_pass`\n   - `p10_gate_allow_fallback_candidates`\n\nIf `run_phase35_backtest.py` lacks parser helper, add a small testable helper only if surgical; otherwise test generated JSON config via quick-mode subprocess if existing test style permits.\n\n## Verification\nRun:\n```powershell\npython -m pytest tests/phase35/test_p10_multi_horizon_blend.py -q\npython -m pytest tests/phase35/ -q\npython scripts/run_phase35_backtest.py --quick-mode --multi-horizon-blend --blend-horizons 1,3,5 --p10-gate-mode relaxed --p10-gate-allow-fallback-candidates\n```\n\n## Report\nWrite `.ly_state/session/l2_p10_gate_tuning_role21_fix_report_20260610.md` mapping F1/F2 to fixes and command results.\n\nDo not commit/push.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":62,"totalLines":62,"truncated":false}},"title":".ly_state\\session\\p10_l2_gate_tuning_role21_fix_prompt_20260610.md","time":{"start":1781046629304,"end":1781046629319}},"id":"prt_eaea6d0540013dZ4621N25K1u1","sessionID":"ses_1515955d6ffegNRB71nAdam01t","messageID":"msg_eaea6ab6a0010p4zn9Da2f4JRq"}}
