{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1781046645796,"sessionID":"ses_1515955d6ffegNRB71nAdam01t","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"tooluse_QPwBxvbjK3TSeiJD8PIgnn","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\GHC\\repos\\OMEGA_QUANT\\.ly_state\\session\\audit_reports\\role21_p10_gate_tuning_audit_20260609.md"},"output":"<path>C:\\Users\\GHC\\repos\\OMEGA_QUANT\\.ly_state\\session\\audit_reports\\role21_p10_gate_tuning_audit_20260609.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Role21 P10 Gate Tuning Audit - 2026-06-09\n2: \n3: ## Gate Contract\n4: \n5: - l3_session_id: role21-p10-gate-tuning-20260609T221500+0700\n6: - l3_session_key: codex:role21:p10-gate-tuning:20260609T221500+0700\n7: - audit_report_path: .ly_state/session/audit_reports/role21_p10_gate_tuning_audit_20260609.md\n8: - final_verdict: [NEEDS_FIX]\n9: \n10: ## Audit Header\n11: \n12: - Role: [L3-Audit:Role21-CodeReviewer]\n13: - Verdict: [NEEDS_FIX]\n14: - PIT Safety: PASS\n15: - Role Compliance: PASS\n16: - Scope: P10 gate tuning changes in `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py`, `scripts/run_phase35_backtest.py`, `tests/phase35/test_p10_multi_horizon_blend.py`, L2 report, relaxed summary JSON.\n17: \n18: ## Findings\n19: \n20: ### F1 - Fallback candidates are still represented as `gated_alphas` downstream\n21: \n22: - Severity: BLOCKER\n23: - Evidence:\n24:   - `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:772-780` falls back to `top_alphas` when all alphas fail Research Gate, then logs and returns them as `gated_alphas`.\n25:   - `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:1291-1299` marks relaxed fallback use only in local logs; no returned/structured flag is carried with the candidate set.\n26:   - `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:1599-1604` stores included horizon details as `gated_alphas` + `gate_results` only.\n27:   - `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:1678-1680` collapses multi-horizon reporting to first horizon `gated_alphas`/`gate_results`; no fallback-candidate source label survives into `FoldMetrics`.\n28:   - `scripts/run_phase35_backtest.py:326-345` persists fold details without gate/fallback candidate diagnostics.\n29:   - Relaxed evidence log shows the mislabel sequence: `Gated alphas (...)` immediately followed by `relaxed gate: using fallback candidates` in `.ly_state/session/p10_tuning_relaxed_20260609/relaxed_h35_train.log:68-80`.\n30: - Impact: Requirement 3 is not fully met. Operators can see fallback use in logs, but persisted artifacts and API-facing fold metrics can still imply failed-gate fallback alphas are true gated alphas.\n31: - Minimal L2 fix: carry a structured label from `_compute_horizon_signal` into `horizon_details`/`FoldMetrics`/JSON, e.g. `selection_source: \"research_gate\" | \"fallback_candidate\"`, `used_fallback_candidates`, `gate_passed_count`, `gate_total`, and avoid naming fallback-only candidates as `gated_alphas` without a source label.\n32: \n33: ### F2 - Required test coverage does not include CLI JSON persistence or fallback labeling\n34: \n35: - Severity: BLOCKER\n36: - Evidence:\n37:   - Collected test list has 36 tests; new `TestP10GateTuning` covers constructor defaults, relaxed/strict engine behavior, invalid mode/min-pass, and non-positive blend quality.\n38:   - No test invokes or unit-tests `scripts/run_phase35_backtest.py` argument parsing / engine argument pass-through / JSON config persistence for `p10_gate_mode`, `p10_gate_min_pass`, `p10_gate_allow_fallback_candidates`.\n39:   - No test asserts fallback candidates are structurally labeled separately from actual gate-passing alphas.\n40: - Impact: Requirement 7 is not met for required item 6 and the structured part of item 3.\n41: - Minimal L2 fix: add script-level test or parser helper test for the three CLI flags and JSON config persistence; add relaxed fallback test asserting the returned/persisted diagnostics label fallback candidates explicitly.\n42: \n43: ## Verified Passes\n44: \n45: - Default strict behavior unchanged: constructor defaults are `strict`, `1`, `False` at `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:190-192`, validation/storage at `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:272-293`, strict excludes zero passes at `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:1275-1280`; unit test covers this at `tests/phase35/test_p10_multi_horizon_blend.py:757-792`.\n46: - Relaxed mode opt-in only: CLI choices/default keep `strict` at `scripts/run_phase35_backtest.py:117-135`; fallback candidates are only considered inside `self.p10_gate_mode == \"relaxed\"` at `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:1280-1303`.\n47: - FAIL strings are not counted as gate passes: `_is_gate_verdict_pass` only accepts `True`, `PASS`, `APPROVED`, and rejects `FAIL*`/unknown strings at `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:37-76`; tests cover FAIL/REJECT/NEEDS_FIX at `tests/phase35/test_p10_multi_horizon_blend.py:492-575`.\n48: - Final-objective signed weighting blocks non-positive quality: final-objective IC is assigned into `train_ic`/`validation_ic` at `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:1349-1368`; blend rejects single/all non-positive quality without `abs(IC)` or equal-weight fallback at `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:1434-1469`; tests cover this at `tests/phase35/test_p10_multi_horizon_blend.py:590-738` and `tests/phase35/test_p10_multi_horizon_blend.py:931-967`.\n49: - Invalid/missing horizons and non-positive blend quality fallback to T+5 baseline: missing return cols return `None` at `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:1214-1217`; all failed/missing and all non-positive quality trigger fallback at `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:1617-1664`.\n50: - CLI flags parse, pass to engine, and are persisted to JSON in implementation: parse at `scripts/run_phase35_backtest.py:117-135`, pass-through at `scripts/run_phase35_backtest.py:244-265`, persisted config at `scripts/run_phase35_backtest.py:288-316`. Manual `--help` check confirmed all flags are exposed.\n51: - Relaxed matrix evidence matches stated candidate: `.ly_state/session/p10_tuning_relaxed_20260609/summary.json` includes `relaxed_h35_train` with IC `0.0005`, RawIC `0.0133`, CSIC `0.0127`, Sharpe `1.4324`, MaxDD `-6.26`, Fallbacks `1`, NonEmptyHorizonFolds `1`, RelaxedCandidateUses `16`.\n52: - PIT safety: no new use of test-period returns in gate decisions or blend weights. Gate/quality metrics are computed from embargoed train/validation slices at `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:1219-1264` and `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:1340-1368`; test-period signal generation remains after gate selection.\n53: \n54: ## Verification Run\n55: \n56: - `python -m pytest tests/phase35/test_p10_multi_horizon_blend.py -q`: 36 passed.\n57: - `python scripts/run_phase35_backtest.py --help | Select-String -Pattern 'p10-gate-mode|p10-gate-min-pass|p10-gate-allow-fallback-candidates|blend-horizons'`: flags present.\n58: - Sample JSON `.ly_state/session/p10_tuning_relaxed_20260609/relaxed_h35_train.json`: config persisted `p10_gate_mode=relaxed`, `p10_gate_min_pass=1`, `p10_gate_allow_fallback_candidates=true`.\n59: \n60: ## Minimal L2 Fixes Required\n61: \n62: 1. Add structured fallback-candidate labeling that survives `_compute_horizon_signal` -> `horizon_details` -> `FoldMetrics`/JSON. Do not expose fallback-only candidates as plain `gated_alphas` without source metadata.\n63: 2. Add tests for structured fallback labeling and CLI flag parse/pass/persist behavior.\n64: \n\n(End of file - total 64 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Role21 P10 Gate Tuning Audit - 2026-06-09\n\n## Gate Contract\n\n- l3_session_id: role21-p10-gate-tuning-20260609T221500+0700\n- l3_session_key: codex:role21:p10-gate-tuning:20260609T221500+0700\n- audit_report_path: .ly_state/session/audit_reports/role21_p10_gate_tuning_audit_20260609.md\n- final_verdict: [NEEDS_FIX]\n\n## Audit Header\n\n- Role: [L3-Audit:Role21-CodeReviewer]\n- Verdict: [NEEDS_FIX]\n- PIT Safety: PASS\n- Role Compliance: PASS\n- Scope: P10 gate tuning changes in `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py`, `scripts/run_phase35_backtest.py`, `tests/phase35/test_p10_multi_horizon_blend.py`, L2 report, relaxed summary JSON.\n\n## Findings\n\n### F1 - Fallback candidates are still represented as `gated_alphas` downstream","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"C:\\Users\\GHC\\repos\\OMEGA_QUANT\\.ly_state\\session\\audit_reports\\role21_p10_gate_tuning_audit_20260609.md","text":"# Role21 P10 Gate Tuning Audit - 2026-06-09\n\n## Gate Contract\n\n- l3_session_id: role21-p10-gate-tuning-20260609T221500+0700\n- l3_session_key: codex:role21:p10-gate-tuning:20260609T221500+0700\n- audit_report_path: .ly_state/session/audit_reports/role21_p10_gate_tuning_audit_20260609.md\n- final_verdict: [NEEDS_FIX]\n\n## Audit Header\n\n- Role: [L3-Audit:Role21-CodeReviewer]\n- Verdict: [NEEDS_FIX]\n- PIT Safety: PASS\n- Role Compliance: PASS\n- Scope: P10 gate tuning changes in `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py`, `scripts/run_phase35_backtest.py`, `tests/phase35/test_p10_multi_horizon_blend.py`, L2 report, relaxed summary JSON.\n\n## Findings\n\n### F1 - Fallback candidates are still represented as `gated_alphas` downstream\n\n- Severity: BLOCKER\n- Evidence:\n  - `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:772-780` falls back to `top_alphas` when all alphas fail Research Gate, then logs and returns them as `gated_alphas`.\n  - `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:1291-1299` marks relaxed fallback use only in local logs; no returned/structured flag is carried with the candidate set.\n  - `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:1599-1604` stores included horizon details as `gated_alphas` + `gate_results` only.\n  - `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:1678-1680` collapses multi-horizon reporting to first horizon `gated_alphas`/`gate_results`; no fallback-candidate source label survives into `FoldMetrics`.\n  - `scripts/run_phase35_backtest.py:326-345` persists fold details without gate/fallback candidate diagnostics.\n  - Relaxed evidence log shows the mislabel sequence: `Gated alphas (...)` immediately followed by `relaxed gate: using fallback candidates` in `.ly_state/session/p10_tuning_relaxed_20260609/relaxed_h35_train.log:68-80`.\n- Impact: Requirement 3 is not fully met. Operators can see fallback use in logs, but persisted artifacts and API-facing fold metrics can still imply failed-gate fallback alphas are true gated alphas.\n- Minimal L2 fix: carry a structured label from `_compute_horizon_signal` into `horizon_details`/`FoldMetrics`/JSON, e.g. `selection_source: \"research_gate\" | \"fallback_candidate\"`, `used_fallback_candidates`, `gate_passed_count`, `gate_total`, and avoid naming fallback-only candidates as `gated_alphas` without a source label.\n\n### F2 - Required test coverage does not include CLI JSON persistence or fallback labeling\n\n- Severity: BLOCKER\n- Evidence:\n  - Collected test list has 36 tests; new `TestP10GateTuning` covers constructor defaults, relaxed/strict engine behavior, invalid mode/min-pass, and non-positive blend quality.\n  - No test invokes or unit-tests `scripts/run_phase35_backtest.py` argument parsing / engine argument pass-through / JSON config persistence for `p10_gate_mode`, `p10_gate_min_pass`, `p10_gate_allow_fallback_candidates`.\n  - No test asserts fallback candidates are structurally labeled separately from actual gate-passing alphas.\n- Impact: Requirement 7 is not met for required item 6 and the structured part of item 3.\n- Minimal L2 fix: add script-level test or parser helper test for the three CLI flags and JSON config persistence; add relaxed fallback test asserting the returned/persisted diagnostics label fallback candidates explicitly.\n\n## Verified Passes\n\n- Default strict behavior unchanged: constructor defaults are `strict`, `1`, `False` at `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:190-192`, validation/storage at `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:272-293`, strict excludes zero passes at `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:1275-1280`; unit test covers this at `tests/phase35/test_p10_multi_horizon_blend.py:757-792`.\n- Relaxed mode opt-in only: CLI choices/default keep `strict` at `scripts/run_phase35_backtest.py:117-135`; fallback candidates are only considered inside `self.p10_gate_mode == \"relaxed\"` at `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:1280-1303`.\n- FAIL strings are not counted as gate passes: `_is_gate_verdict_pass` only accepts `True`, `PASS`, `APPROVED`, and rejects `FAIL*`/unknown strings at `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:37-76`; tests cover FAIL/REJECT/NEEDS_FIX at `tests/phase35/test_p10_multi_horizon_blend.py:492-575`.\n- Final-objective signed weighting blocks non-positive quality: final-objective IC is assigned into `train_ic`/`validation_ic` at `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:1349-1368`; blend rejects single/all non-positive quality without `abs(IC)` or equal-weight fallback at `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:1434-1469`; tests cover this at `tests/phase35/test_p10_multi_horizon_blend.py:590-738` and `tests/phase35/test_p10_multi_horizon_blend.py:931-967`.\n- Invalid/missing horizons and non-positive blend quality fallback to T+5 baseline: missing return cols return `None` at `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:1214-1217`; all failed/missing and all non-positive quality trigger fallback at `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:1617-1664`.\n- CLI flags parse, pass to engine, and are persisted to JSON in implementation: parse at `scripts/run_phase35_backtest.py:117-135`, pass-through at `scripts/run_phase35_backtest.py:244-265`, persisted config at `scripts/run_phase35_backtest.py:288-316`. Manual `--help` check confirmed all flags are exposed.\n- Relaxed matrix evidence matches stated candidate: `.ly_state/session/p10_tuning_relaxed_20260609/summary.json` includes `relaxed_h35_train` with IC `0.0005`, RawIC `0.0133`, CSIC `0.0127`, Sharpe `1.4324`, MaxDD `-6.26`, Fallbacks `1`, NonEmptyHorizonFolds `1`, RelaxedCandidateUses `16`.\n- PIT safety: no new use of test-period returns in gate decisions or blend weights. Gate/quality metrics are computed from embargoed train/validation slices at `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:1219-1264` and `src/omega/quant/phase35_walk_forward.py:1340-1368`; test-period signal generation remains after gate selection.\n\n## Verification Run\n\n- `python -m pytest tests/phase35/test_p10_multi_horizon_blend.py -q`: 36 passed.\n- `python scripts/run_phase35_backtest.py --help | Select-String -Pattern 'p10-gate-mode|p10-gate-min-pass|p10-gate-allow-fallback-candidates|blend-horizons'`: flags present.\n- Sample JSON `.ly_state/session/p10_tuning_relaxed_20260609/relaxed_h35_train.json`: config persisted `p10_gate_mode=relaxed`, `p10_gate_min_pass=1`, `p10_gate_allow_fallback_candidates=true`.\n\n## Minimal L2 Fixes Required\n\n1. Add structured fallback-candidate labeling that survives `_compute_horizon_signal` -> `horizon_details` -> `FoldMetrics`/JSON. Do not expose fallback-only candidates as plain `gated_alphas` without source metadata.\n2. Add tests for structured fallback labeling and CLI flag parse/pass/persist behavior.\n","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":64,"totalLines":64,"truncated":false}},"title":".ly_state\\session\\audit_reports\\role21_p10_gate_tuning_audit_20260609.md","time":{"start":1781046645788,"end":1781046645794}},"id":"prt_eaea711d6001PHI1Voiw1ibq1S","sessionID":"ses_1515955d6ffegNRB71nAdam01t","messageID":"msg_eaea6fd0f001cuqZ3NkgmI7Uce"}}
