{"type":"text","timestamp":1781047014214,"sessionID":"ses_1515955d6ffegNRB71nAdam01t","part":{"id":"prt_eaeac71aa001C8E84e625zoFkv","messageID":"msg_eaeac6378001X5OHibxxJCyGo6","sessionID":"ses_1515955d6ffegNRB71nAdam01t","type":"text","text":"<thinking>\nGood! I've successfully completed F1.4: Update FoldMetrics instantiation to pass gate_metadata. Now let me update the todo list and move on to F1.5: Update fallback logic and logging.\n\nF1.5 is about updating the fallback logic in `validate_alpha_with_research_gate` to improve logging. Looking at the audit report, line 780 says:\n\n```python\nlogger.info(f\"Gated alphas ({len(gated_alphas)}/{len(top_alphas)}): {gated_alphas}\")\n```\n\nThe issue is that when fallback happens (lines 772-778), the code still logs these as \"Gated alphas\" even though they're fallback candidates that didn't actually pass the gate. The task says to \"adjust log wording if easy: avoid saying fallback-only candidates are truly gated; e.g. `Selected alphas` or include source in log.\"\n\nHowever, the fallback logic at lines 772-780 is in the `validate_alpha_with_research_gate` function which doesn't know about the P10 gate tuning context (strict vs relaxed mode). The P10-specific fallback logic is in `_compute_horizon_signal` at lines 1280-1322, and I've already addressed that by including selection_source in the gate_metadata and updating the log at the end of `_compute_horizon_signal` to include `selection_source`.\n\nFor the fallback at line 772-780 in `validate_alpha_with_research_gate`, this is the old fallback logic that happens when ALL alphas fail the gate. This is different from the P10 relaxed mode fallback.\n\nLooking at the task requirements again:\n\"Also adjust log wording if easy: avoid saying fallback-only candidates are truly gated; e.g. `Selected alphas` or include source in log.\"\n\nI think the simple fix here is to change the log message at line 780 to be more neutral, like \"Selected alphas\" instead of \"Gated alphas\", or to add a note when fallback was used.\n\nActually, looking at the code more carefully, the fallback at lines 772-778 sets gated_alphas to top_alphas, then at line 780 it logs them. I could add conditional logging here to distinguish between fallback and actual gate passes.\n\nLet me make a simple change to improve the logging clarity. I'll read that section again and then update it.\n</thinking>","time":{"start":1781046997418,"end":1781047014211}}}
